== Ranged Stance ==

Most of the other stances are fairly straightforward, but this stance seems to cause a lot of confusion. While Berserkers, Monks and Rogues also get this stance, Rangers are the only class likely to make heavy use of this due to two other Ranger benefits: Innate Called Shot and Weapon Mastery of the Scout.  Innate Called Shot is granted free at level 1 and causes Rangers to get "Double Shots" (double damage) on any target that is not moving. Weapon Mastery of the Scout, at Rank 3, increases all bow damage by 100%.  These two AAs cause Rangers to do quadruple damage (against stationary targets) with bows compared to every other class.

Benefits of Ranged Stance:
*Your Ranged Attacks have no minimum distance.
**Pretty self explanatory - you can use your bow as your weapon while in melee range. You must leave Ranged Stance if you want to go back to using your melee weapons. 
*Grants +25% Accuracy
**This likely gives your Ranged Accuracy stat a 25% boost, but since Ranged Accuracy is not displayed anywhere like main hand accuracy is, there's no way to confirm directly.
**However, testing has shown that a level 34 ranger against a level 40 target goes from a ~59% hit rate to ~67% hit rate with Ranged stance, so it does work.
**This benefit is more significant against creatures who have high AC relative to your Attack. Against weaker targets you won't see much change in hit rate.
*Your Ranged Attacks <em>can</em> double and triple attack.
**This is the one that seems to cause the most confusion. Under normal conditions, ranged attacks do not use the Double Attack and Triple Attack skills. You can have 200 Double Attack skill, shoot your bow all day and never get a double attack. When you are in Ranged Stance, your ranged attacks will make use of your Double Attack and Triple Attack skill. However, if you don't yet have Double Attack (level 20 for Rangers) or Triple Attack (level 46 for Rangers) you will never get double or triple attacks with Ranged Stance because your skill is 0.
**This benefit is huge. With only 175 Double Attack Skill, your bow attacks will Double Attack 40-50% of the time, and that's not even max skill, nor does it include Triple attacks. This is a big boost to archery damage, especially combined the the Ranger bow AAs mentioned above.

